parameter.description:
If neither a {{param}} nor {{param|CABundle}} is provided to this command and an entry exists in {{object|Device.Security.ClientCertificateDefault.{i}}}
with {{param|Device.Security.ClientCertificateDefault.{i}.Type}} matching this command, then the Certificate and CABundle values will be used from
{{object|Device.Security.ClientCertificateDefault.}}.

If neither a {{param|Certificate}} nor {{param}} is provided to this command and an entry exists in {{object|Device.Security.ClientCertificateDefault.{i}}}
with {{param|Device.Security.ClientCertificateDefault.{i}.Type}} matching this command, then the Certificate and CABundle values will be used from
{{object|Device.Security.ClientCertificateDefault.}}.

The Issuer field in an X.509 certificate, see {{bibref|RFC5280}};
i.e. the Distinguished Name (DN) of the entity who has signed the
certificate.

Specifies the automatic certificate update mode. When auto-update
is triggered, certificate information is copied from {{object}}
to populate the new CSR.
